From f422f8d5f2bccc3e3a42a0abff370375d6ed32a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:58:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] media: rkvdec: set the streaming DMA mask

RKVDEC writes buffer addresses to 32-bit hardware registers, but probe
sets only the coherent DMA mask. Imported vb2 DMABUFs are mapped
through the streaming DMA API and use dev->dma_mask, so the coherent
mask does not constrain those addresses.

Set the streaming and coherent masks together to keep every
hardware-visible mapping within the 32-bit aperture.

Fixes: cd33c830448b ("media: rkvdec: Add the rkvdec driver")
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 054eb8a366df1..3f90228b66561 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1900,9 +1900,9 @@ static int rkvdec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return PTR_ERR(rkvdec->link);
 	}
 
-	ret = dma_set_coherent_mask(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(&pdev->dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Could not set DMA coherent mask.\n");
+		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Could not set DMA mask.\n");
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-- 
